<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26462" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭbentĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭb-</span></b> ), ae,
			f.
		libens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>delight, pleasure, joy</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onustum pectus porto laetitia lubentiaque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Stich. 2, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">postquam erili filio Largitu's dictis dapsilis
					lubentias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Ps. 1, 4, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libentiae gratiaeque conviviorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					15, 2, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Personified: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lĭbentĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lŭb-</span></b> ),
			ae, f., <i>the goddess of
				delight</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 2, 2</span></i>; cf. the foll.
			art.</div>
